WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.430
It was late October of 1993 and John Matthews
of Myrtle Beach, South Carolina had just scored

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:11.210
a date with Sarah, one of the most popular
girls in school, and he had planned the perfect

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.589
night out for the two of them.

00:00:12.589 --> 00:00:17.830
A haunted house had just been set up in town,
and he, like many guys before him, figured

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.859
he could use that as a chance to impress his
date.

00:00:20.859 --> 00:00:24.830
He'd already been through the attraction,
so he knew exactly when to put his arm around

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:29.520
Sarah when one of the costumed actors or animatronics
tried to spook them.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.540
If any of them got too close for comfort,
he might even punch them, just to show Sarah

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.680
how brave he was.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.510
That would be a sure-fire way to impress any
girl.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:45.260
However, John had no idea of the real horror
that waited for him and his date through the

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.600
doors of this seemingly normal fun-house.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.800
At first, the haunted house went as normal.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.890
John laughed at all the fake cobwebs and plastic
skeletons, making sure Sarah knew how dumb

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:56.960
he thought they looked.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.330
He shoved away actors dressed as axe murderers
and told them to stay away from his date.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:07.310
It was dark, so they couldn't really see each
other's faces, but John guessed that Sarah

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.439
was probably really impressed.

00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:14.380
All in all, the date was going well, until
they got to a room that John hadn't seen the

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.210
first time he'd been through.

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:20.920
It seemed like it had been added overnight,
but at the same time, it didn't mesh with

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:21.920
the theme.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.030
The theme of the haunted house this year was
“cannibal hotel”, but this room looked

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:31.750
more like Dracula's castle, complete with
actors dressed as Frankenstein, the wolf man,

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.689
and Dracula himself.

00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:37.110
One of them was even a dead ringer for actor
Vincent Price.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:43.549
John and Sarah watched, confused, as the actors
performed their routine which, just like their

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:45.679
surroundings, seemed out of place.

00:01:45.679 --> 00:01:50.679
It was totally hackneyed, full of lame puns
and very basic scares, though the special

00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:53.479
effects were undeniably impressive.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:57.320
When John and Sarah walked through the room,
the actor dressed as Dracula stood in front

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.060
of John and started pretending to hypnotize
him.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:05.289
Up close, he did look a lot like Bela Lugosi
- the actor who’d portrayed The Count during

00:02:05.289 --> 00:02:07.749
his first big screen appearance.

00:02:07.749 --> 00:02:13.080
This definitely threw John off a little, but
unfortunately, this Dracula didn't have Lugosi's

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.170
acting talents.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.850
“You are under my control.”

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:20.940
Dracula said, waving his fingers at John and
staring at him.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.390
John, getting really sick of this, pushed
the guy out of the way to move on to the next

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.390
room.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:30.570
But when he did, he felt that something was
really, really wrong here.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:35.170
He practically dragged Sarah away from watching
the wolf man transform and ran the rest of

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.850
the way through the house, all of his bravado
now gone.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.940
Sarah asked her date what was wrong, and he
didn't tell her.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.400
How could he, without sounding crazy?

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.760
When he had touched that actor playing Dracula,
something hadn't felt right.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:52.860
Even through his suit and cape, John had been
able to tell that wrong.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:58.780
He was cold, and rigid, not like a human being,
but like a robot, or a wax dummy.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:03.590
This is just one of multiple complaints from
Halloween attractions around the United States

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.090
that prompted the action of the SCP Foundation.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:11.480
Several witnesses described either seeing
people that resembled classic movie monsters,

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:17.580
or living wax models of those monsters, appearing
in various haunted houses, corn mazes, carnivals,

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.690
and strip malls across the country.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:25.920
The Foundation has designated this troupe
of hammy wax actors SCP-4153.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:32.370
During performances, SCP-4153 use wax to alter
their appearance, produce props - including

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:36.380
fake blood and gore - and even manipulate
wax objects from afar.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:41.510
While this results in some uncanny special
effects, the content of the performances tend

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:44.420
to be pretty standard, classic haunted house
fare.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:49.180
They mostly do things like reenacting scenes
from classic horror films, and telling “spooky”

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:52.130
jokes, with a little fake blood here and there.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:55.880
When the Foundation arrived at the Myrtle
Beach attraction they apprehended the various

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:00.630
wax characters, and determined that their
eerie resemblance to the classic horror characters

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.510
wasn't just makeup.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:06.270
After the horrors some of these Foundation
employees had seen on the job, living wax

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:11.250
models of Frankenstein's monster and Dracula
seemed almost cute in comparison, and the

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:16.100
troupe of wax actors were taken to Site 9
for questioning and containment.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:22.849
The first member of the troupe to be interviewed
on-site was Dracula, dubbed SCP-4153-017 by

00:04:22.849 --> 00:04:23.849
the Foundation.

00:04:23.849 --> 00:04:28.430
He was interviewed by Agent Timothy West,
who was totally unimpressed with Dracula's

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:29.430
schtick.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:34.050
He tried to hypnotize Agent West, an act which
he flatly refused to indulge in.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:38.460
Dracula provided the agent with seemingly
no useful information, only responding to

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:44.509
questions with clichés like “We were all
dead, the whole time.” and “The log was

00:04:44.509 --> 00:04:47.080
coming from inside the house.”

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:53.650
The next wax figure to be interrogated was
Frankenstein's monster, aka SCP-4153-015,

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:57.379
who was interviewed by Agent Samantha Henwick.

00:04:57.379 --> 00:05:05.129
Much like how SCP-4153-017 stayed fully in
character as Dracula during his interview,

00:05:05.129 --> 00:05:11.389
SCP-4153-015 seemed to really believe that
he was actor Boris Karloff, who played Frankenstein's

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:14.169
monster in the 1930's.

00:05:14.169 --> 00:05:19.789
The SCP spoke in an exact imitation of Karloff's
voice and speech patterns, and talked to Agent

00:05:19.789 --> 00:05:22.849
Henwick as if she was another actor on a movie
set.

00:05:22.849 --> 00:05:27.930
He talked about how honored he was to be part
of “the project” and asked “are we rolling?”

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.349
when he noticed the conversation was being
recorded.

00:05:30.349 --> 00:05:35.159
Agent Henwick responded to the SCP's comments
with confusion, a fact which he took to mean

00:05:35.159 --> 00:05:37.410
that she was “staying in character”.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:42.160
Like a true actor, he took a moment to prepare
himself before pulling his own head off, much

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:44.319
to the horror of Agent Henwick.

00:05:44.319 --> 00:05:48.999
The last and probably most interesting of
the interviews conducted in 1993 was with

00:05:48.999 --> 00:05:54.879
the wax figure who resembled Vincent Price,
more specifically Vincent Price in his role

00:05:54.879 --> 00:06:01.849
as Henry Jarrod in 1953's House of Wax - a
movie about a mad sculptor who made wax figures

00:06:01.849 --> 00:06:04.439
out of the corpses of his victims.

00:06:04.439 --> 00:06:12.250
This wax figure was designated SCP-4153-036,
and was interviewed by Agent Gerald Penn.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:17.449
Penn started the interview with a simple question-
why do you try to frighten people?

00:06:17.449 --> 00:06:23.809
SCP-4153-036 had an equally simple answer-
“Why does anyone try to frighten?

00:06:23.809 --> 00:06:25.620
It's fun to be frightened.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:29.050
Almost as much fun as it is to do the frightening.”

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:33.629
Penn was skeptical, pointing out that the
wax figures' act wasn't especially frightening.

00:06:33.629 --> 00:06:39.330
The SCP laughed dismissively, telling Penn
to “have some respect for the classics.”

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.419
Penn was still not having any of it.

00:06:41.419 --> 00:06:46.960
He'd been with the SCP foundation for 20 years
at this point, and he'd seen enough real horror

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.309
that the so-called 'classics' had no effect
on him whatsoever.

00:06:51.309 --> 00:06:53.289
He pressured Price for answers.

00:06:53.289 --> 00:06:57.439
But Instead of responding with a straight
answer, Price launched into a speech about

00:06:57.439 --> 00:06:59.360
his feelings on monsters.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:05.370
He said “You'll call any oaf with a steak-knife
hunting gaggles of teens a monster, these

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:06.370
days.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:08.340
There's no wit, no humor, no charm.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.680
Where's the passion?

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:10.789
The artisanship?

00:07:10.789 --> 00:07:11.789
Where's the sense of theater?

00:07:11.789 --> 00:07:14.159
Would you like to know something peculiar?

00:07:14.159 --> 00:07:16.000
I've almost never played a monster.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.189
Oh, I've played villains, most certainly!

00:07:18.189 --> 00:07:20.080
But not monsters.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.689
Only men, besieged by fate, driven to revenge.

00:07:23.689 --> 00:07:26.259
Still — I've always had a fondness for them.

00:07:26.259 --> 00:07:31.189
Even as a child, I sympathized more with the
monster than the hero.”

00:07:31.189 --> 00:07:35.530
Agent Penn, who, at this point, was really
getting tired of all the theatrics started

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:40.460
to interject, but when he opened his mouth
to speak he was only able to get a few words

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:44.580
out before his tongue went numb and rigid
in his mouth.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.319
He could no longer move it.

00:07:46.319 --> 00:07:50.889
Agent Penn tried to speak, but his tongue
was too solid and heavy to do anything more

00:07:50.889 --> 00:07:53.839
than knock uselessly against his bottom teeth.

00:07:53.839 --> 00:07:57.610
He felt something dislodge inside his mouth,
and hoped maybe that it was the feeling of

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:01.740
his tongue being freed from whatever spell
the SCP had put it under.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:07.559
But then he started to feel a tearing, and
a sticky heaviness in his bottom jaw.

00:08:07.559 --> 00:08:09.979
Agent Penn reached up and felt around inside
his mouth.

00:08:09.979 --> 00:08:14.979
He started to scream indistinctly when he
realized, to his horror, that his tongue had

00:08:14.979 --> 00:08:15.979
ripped off.

00:08:15.979 --> 00:08:20.910
He pulled it out of his mouth, and when he
held it in his hand, his fears were confirmed

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:25.759
- somehow, it had become nothing more than
a lump of pink wax.

00:08:25.759 --> 00:08:30.869
Now completely tongueless, Agent Penn continued
to babble frantically, no doubt trying to

00:08:30.869 --> 00:08:36.409
curse at the wax creature sitting in front
of him.

00:08:36.409 --> 00:08:39.529
SCP-4153-036 finally paid attention to his
interviewer's distress at this point.

00:08:39.529 --> 00:08:44.769
He turned to Agent Penn with a look of disapproval
and disappointment and said,“Oh dear.

00:08:44.769 --> 00:08:47.750
Your tongue seems to have gotten away from
you, there.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.389
Here — allow me.”

00:08:49.389 --> 00:08:54.310
The SCP leaned towards Agent Penn, and though
the agent wanted to resist, he found that

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:56.440
he could no longer move his arms.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:09:01.790
In fact, his whole body had gone numb and
rigid, just like the wax tongue.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:06.440
The only movement he was capable of was opening
his mouth as the wax facsimile of Vincent

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:11.640
Price started molding his tongue back to the
proper shape, and reattached it inside of

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.160
Agent Penn's mouth.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:17.399
Agent Penn whimpered, unable to do anything
while the SCP's hands were in his mouth.

00:09:17.399 --> 00:09:18.820
The creature said, “Hush, now.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:24.130
I warned you about this — I told you that
you mustn't disturb the wax before it hardens.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:27.050
That is a crucial part of the process.

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:28.850
It needs to solidify.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:32.269
Otherwise, you risk disturbing the performance.”

00:09:32.269 --> 00:09:37.699
By the time his tongue was reattached and
resealed, Agent Penn was on the verge of tears.

00:09:37.699 --> 00:09:42.139
He gurgled, gasping for air, wiggling his
tongue around in his mouth to make sure that

00:09:42.139 --> 00:09:43.139
it worked.

00:09:43.139 --> 00:09:46.390
The SCP returned to his seat, pleased with
his own handiwork.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:47.470
“Splendid, splendid.

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:49.079
Good as new....

00:09:49.079 --> 00:09:52.149
Now, let's take it from the top, shall we?”

00:09:52.149 --> 00:10:00.000
Agent Penn took a deep breath, steadying himself,
as SCP-4153-036 whispered the word “action.”

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:08.230
Penn resumed the interview with the same simple
question - why do you try to frighten people?

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:12.730
SCP-4153-036 gave the same simple answer-
“Why does anyone try to frighten?

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:14.579
It's fun to be frightened.

00:10:14.579 --> 00:10:17.019
Almost as much fun as it is to do the frightening.”

00:10:17.019 --> 00:10:22.180
The interview continued for only a few minutes
longer, with both parties repeating only things

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:24.161
they'd said earlier in the recording.

00:10:24.161 --> 00:10:31.560
The log ends with SCP-4153-036 once again
saying “Have some respect for the classics.”

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:36.720
Not long after that interview concluded, Foundation
management completely lost contact with Site

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:37.720
9.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:42.430
A Mobile Task Force was sent in to investigate
the cause of this loss of contact, and upon

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:45.940
arrival they found a catastrophic containment
breach.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:51.699
Not a single member of on-site personnel was
found alive, and strangely, all of their bodies

00:10:51.699 --> 00:10:54.160
seemed to be coated in wax.

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:58.339
Further examination revealed that this initial
observation wasn’t the case at all.

00:10:58.339 --> 00:11:00.810
They weren’t just coated in wax.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:05.940
No, every member of the site 9 team had had
all of their major organs, including their

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:10.360
skin, surgically extracted and replaced with
sculpted wax.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:16.019
Of course this was assumed to be the doing
of SCP-4153, but oddly, all of the autopsies

00:11:16.019 --> 00:11:22.899
suggested that the removal of organs had happened
weeks before the apprehension of SCP-4153,

00:11:22.899 --> 00:11:27.630
even though all of the site personnel had
seemed alive and well right up until the containment

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:28.630
breach.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:33.540
Outside of being replaced by wax, no damage
was done to the bodies - it seemed that everyone

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.470
had just dropped dead at the same time.

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:41.320
There was one body that was different though
- that of Agent Gerald Penn.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:45.190
Agent Penn’s decapitated body was found
in the same containment cell that had been

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:49.740
used for SCP-4153-036.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:56.079
Next to the body was a photograph showing
SCP-4153-036 holding up Agent Penn's screaming

00:11:56.079 --> 00:12:03.560
head and on the back, a single sentence was
written - From one horror aficionado to another:

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:05.050
Always Stay A-Head!

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:12.769
All of the SCP-4153 instances remain unaccounted
for, and MTF Iota-10, also known as the “Damn

00:12:12.769 --> 00:12:17.270
Feds” continue to monitor for new sightings
and reports of activity that may be linked

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:18.790
to the wax troupe.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:23.649
Hopefully one day they’ll be taken into
Foundation and contained, and maybe all it

00:12:23.649 --> 00:12:29.850
will take is for them to meet someone with
a sufficient appreciation for “the classics.”

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:35.079
Now for something from the more terrifying
archives of the SCP Foundation Check out “SCP

00:12:35.079 --> 00:12:39.990
– 096 - The Shy Guy” or “SCP-106 - The
Old Man”

